\subsection{5th-Order WENO-Z Characteristic Reconstruction}
To suppress spurious Gibbs oscillations across relativistic blast waves without introducing excess numerical diffusion in laminar zones, interface variables $v_{i+1/2}^{\pm}$ are reconstructed using non-linear WENO-Z weights. Given a 5-point stencil $(v_{i-2}, v_{i-1}, v_i, v_{i+1}, v_{i+2})$, the three 3rd-order substencils are:
\begin{align}
    p_0 &= \frac{1}{3} v_{i-2} - \frac{7}{6} v_{i-1} + \frac{11}{6} v_i \\
    p_1 &= -\frac{1}{6} v_{i-1} + \frac{5}{6} v_i + \frac{1}{3} v_{i+1} \\
    p_2 &= \frac{1}{3} v_i + \frac{5}{6} v_{i+1} - \frac{1}{6} v_{i+2}
\end{align}
The Jiang-Shu smoothness indicators $\beta_k$ are evaluated via:
\begin{align}
    \beta_0 &= \frac{13}{12}(v_{i-2} - 2v_{i-1} + v_i)^2 + \frac{1}{4}(v_{i-2} - 4v_{i-1} + 3v_i)^2 \\
    \beta_1 &= \frac{13}{12}(v_{i-1} - 2v_i + v_{i+1})^2 + \frac{1}{4}(v_{i-1} - v_{i+1})^2 \\
    \beta_2 &= \frac{13}{12}(v_i - 2v_{i+1} + v_{i+2})^2 + \frac{1}{4}(3v_i - 4v_{i+1} + v_{i+2})^2
\end{align}
The global 5th-order smoothness indicator is $\tau_5 = |\beta_0 - \beta_2|$. The WENO-Z non-linear weights $\omega_k$ are computed as:
\begin{equation}
    \alpha_k = d_k \left[ 1 + \left( \frac{\tau_5}{\beta_k + \epsilon} \right)^2 \right], \quad \omega_k = \frac{\alpha_k}{\sum_{j=0}^2 \alpha_j}
\end{equation}
where $d_0 = 0.1$, $d_1 = 0.6$, $d_2 = 0.3$, and $\epsilon = 10^{-40}$. The left reconstructed state is $v_{i+1/2}^L = \sum_{k=0}^2 \omega_k p_k$.

